    "summary": "On the dying planet of the Ninth House, the indentured orphan Gideon Nav trains with swords and dreams of escape, while the Reverend Daughter Harrowhark Nonagesimus prepares to answer the Emperor's summons. The Emperor has called the heirs of the nine Houses to Canaan House to compete to become Lyctors, immortal necromantic hands of the Emperor. Each heir must bring a cavalier, a sworn sword. Harrow, a bone necromancer, forces Gideon into the role. At Canaan House the pairs explore locked rooms, decipher a puzzle, and fight monsters and each other. ||Gideon dies to save Harrow during the fight with the resurrected Lyctor Cytherea, and Harrow absorbs her soul, becoming a Lyctor.||",
